1
00:01:43,220 --> 00:01:48,020
[When I Meet The Moon]

2
00:01:48,210 --> 00:01:51,030
[Episode 6]

3
00:02:06,430 --> 00:02:07,930
Thanks... Thank you.

4
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:24,360
Well, this is...

5
00:02:26,370 --> 00:02:27,370
From the company.

6
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:30,120
Thank you.

7
00:02:39,020 --> 00:02:40,249
I was starving,

8
00:02:40,250 --> 00:02:41,810
so I ate another portion.

9
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:50,150
Did I take his portion?

10
00:02:55,780 --> 00:02:57,970
I'm also quite hungry today.

11
00:03:00,650 --> 00:03:02,580
W-Well, then, you should eat more.

12
00:03:33,370 --> 00:03:34,120
Since you're done,

13
00:03:34,121 --> 00:03:36,320
I'll throw your wrapper away with mine.

14
00:05:12,770 --> 00:05:13,770
Thanks.

15
00:05:22,930 --> 00:05:23,990
Put this on to avoid

16
00:05:24,060 --> 00:05:25,060
catching a cold.

17
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:30,430
Let me dry you, too.

18
00:05:43,900 --> 00:05:44,930
I'll do it myself.

19
00:06:26,250 --> 00:06:27,000
Feifei,

20
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:28,749
since you're on field duty today,

21
00:06:28,750 --> 00:06:30,099
you can get off work early.

22
00:06:30,100 --> 00:06:31,330
Thanks, Mr. Qin.

23
00:06:31,390 --> 00:06:32,720
I'll take my leave then.

24
00:06:32,860 --> 00:06:34,660
See you next week, Mr. Qin.
See you next week.

25
00:06:41,810 --> 00:06:42,810
Yun Li!

26
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:47,800
Come over here.

27
00:06:55,450 --> 00:06:56,450
Mr. Qin.

28
00:06:58,240 --> 00:06:59,500
This is urgent.

29
00:06:59,630 --> 00:07:00,860
Help me sort out

30
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:01,890
the player feedback

31
00:07:01,891 --> 00:07:03,299
from the experience center.

32
00:07:03,300 --> 00:07:04,979
I need them for tomorrow's meeting.

33
00:07:04,980 --> 00:07:07,189
You need so many of them sorted out today?

34
00:07:07,190 --> 00:07:09,659
The R&D department needs
a large sample of data,

35
00:07:09,660 --> 00:07:10,799
and they need it urgently.

36
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:12,200
Just work some overtime.

37
00:07:12,750 --> 00:07:13,930
Go for it, Yun Li.

38
00:07:17,830 --> 00:07:19,250
"Go for it, Yun Li."

39
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:21,700
How could he even say that?

40
00:07:29,630 --> 00:07:30,630
You're back.

41
00:07:31,390 --> 00:07:33,069
It's pouring rain outside, isn't it?

42
00:07:33,070 --> 00:07:34,070
Dry yourself.
Thanks.

43
00:07:35,310 --> 00:07:36,310
Everything about Nanwu is great,

44
00:07:36,311 --> 00:07:37,919
except for the frequent rain.

45
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:38,870
That's just how Nanwu is,

46
00:07:38,871 --> 00:07:39,949
with endless rain.

47
00:07:39,950 --> 00:07:41,389
Hurry back to your room, take a hot shower,

48
00:07:41,390 --> 00:07:42,650
and get some good rest.

49
00:07:42,680 --> 00:07:43,680
Thank you.

50
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:47,360
Good night.

51
00:07:53,600 --> 00:07:54,720
Fu Zhengchu.

52
00:07:58,190 --> 00:07:59,190
What's wrong?

53
00:07:59,270 --> 00:08:01,189
What happened between you and Tangy?

54
00:08:01,190 --> 00:08:02,870
What do you mean?
What happened between us?

55
00:08:02,950 --> 00:08:04,150
Check the group chat.

56
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:05,930
What on earth happened?

57
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:11,360
Where's Lili?

58
00:08:12,270 --> 00:08:13,869
She's still not off work yet?

59
00:08:13,870 --> 00:08:14,560
Nope.

60
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:16,479
If I can't afford to mess
with her, I can at least hide.

61
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:17,480
Fu Zhengchu!

62
00:08:18,950 --> 00:08:19,950
What's up?

63
00:08:20,430 --> 00:08:21,490
Give me your phone.

64
00:08:21,870 --> 00:08:22,560
What for?

65
00:08:22,720 --> 00:08:23,720
Your phone.

66
00:08:23,950 --> 00:08:24,950
Hurry!

67
00:08:25,870 --> 00:08:26,950
Tangy, your phone.

68
00:08:28,430 --> 00:08:29,509
What's this all about?

69
00:08:29,510 --> 00:08:30,950
You two, add each other

70
00:08:31,020 --> 00:08:32,909
on WeChat right now,

71
00:08:33,270 --> 00:08:35,870
so you won't bother me
with every little thing.

72
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:38,080
Done.

73
00:09:04,390 --> 00:09:05,390
Finished.

74
00:09:05,860 --> 00:09:06,750
Awesome, Yun Li,

75
00:09:06,751 --> 00:09:08,200
you finished all of them.

76
00:09:08,730 --> 00:09:10,010
Save, save...

77
00:09:14,770 --> 00:09:15,940
It's this late?

78
00:09:18,500 --> 00:09:19,500
The last bus...

79
00:09:19,720 --> 00:09:20,820
I won't make it.

80
00:09:59,590 --> 00:10:00,590
Wait a minute!

81
00:10:04,670 --> 00:10:05,670
Wait...

82
00:11:41,270 --> 00:11:43,269
It's 10 o'clock! The special offers start!

83
00:11:43,270 --> 00:11:45,839
- 20% off for all the soon-to-expire items.
- Wel...

84
00:11:45,840 --> 00:11:47,619
-Welcome... -Spend a little for a feast!

85
00:11:47,620 --> 00:11:49,009
Miss it, and you'll have
to wait for tomorrow's.

86
00:11:49,010 --> 00:11:50,340
Come and grab a bargain!

87
00:12:10,310 --> 00:12:11,310
Hello.

88
00:12:18,170 --> 00:12:19,370
I didn't get this.

89
00:12:20,400 --> 00:12:21,410
It's a free gift.

90
00:12:21,890 --> 00:12:22,890
Thank you.

91
00:12:27,460 --> 00:12:28,360
Sorry,

92
00:12:28,390 --> 00:12:30,320
I didn't know you were at work today

93
00:12:30,390 --> 00:12:32,390
and didn't bring the umbrella over.

94
00:12:32,600 --> 00:12:34,240
It's okay. No rush.

95
00:12:36,790 --> 00:12:38,549
Did you just start working here?

96
00:12:38,550 --> 00:12:40,239
How come I haven't seen you before?

97
00:12:40,240 --> 00:12:41,300
Yeah, I'm new here.

98
00:12:42,630 --> 00:12:43,839
Then I'll return the umbrella

99
00:12:43,840 --> 00:12:45,130
to you next time I come.

100
00:12:45,700 --> 00:12:46,700
Deal.

101
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:48,080
Do you want...
No, thank you.

102
00:12:52,750 --> 00:12:54,060
To add me on WeChat...

103
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:16,200
Lili,

104
00:13:16,290 --> 00:13:17,789
what time did you get home last night?

105
00:13:17,790 --> 00:13:19,549
Why didn't you reply to my messages again?

106
00:13:19,550 --> 00:13:21,100
I probably fell asleep.

107
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:23,440
What's up with your voice?

108
00:13:23,670 --> 00:13:24,800
Did you catch a cold?

109
00:13:25,650 --> 00:13:26,790
Probably.

110
00:13:27,340 --> 00:13:28,719
Then you should get some good rest at home

111
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:30,120
instead of going to work.

112
00:13:30,150 --> 00:13:31,859
I just started working,
and I'm asking for leave?

113
00:13:31,860 --> 00:13:32,990
Is that really okay?

114
00:13:33,290 --> 00:13:35,490
I'll be fine after drinking more water.

115
00:13:35,960 --> 00:13:36,760
Where are you?

116
00:13:36,790 --> 00:13:38,390
I'll send you some medicine.

117
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:40,130
I'm on my way.

118
00:13:40,150 --> 00:13:41,150
Almost there.

119
00:13:41,550 --> 00:13:43,210
Don't push yourself too hard.

120
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:44,200
Tell me anytime

121
00:13:44,201 --> 00:13:45,400
if anything happens.

122
00:13:45,460 --> 00:13:46,250
I got it.

123
00:13:46,251 --> 00:13:47,650
I'll listen to you, boss.

124
00:13:48,100 --> 00:13:49,100
Bye-bye.

125
00:14:05,840 --> 00:14:07,970
If my skateboard doesn't arrive soon,

126
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:10,439
running a marathon like this every day

127
00:14:10,440 --> 00:14:11,790
will kill me first.

128
00:14:24,770 --> 00:14:25,770
Hello?

129
00:14:26,150 --> 00:14:27,150
Where are you?

130
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:28,740
What do you mean?

131
00:14:29,390 --> 00:14:30,230
I mean,

132
00:14:30,260 --> 00:14:32,190
where are you right now?

133
00:14:32,460 --> 00:14:34,530
I'm... in the classroom.

134
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:36,790
Panting like that,

135
00:14:36,791 --> 00:14:38,289
you say you're in the classroom?

136
00:14:38,290 --> 00:14:39,290
Turn around.

137
00:14:39,500 --> 00:14:40,500
Turn around?

138
00:14:45,190 --> 00:14:46,190
Get on.

139
00:14:47,660 --> 00:14:49,466
Your bike doesn't have a rear seat.
Where do I get on?

140
00:14:49,490 --> 00:14:50,490
Cut the crap.

141
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:51,390
Get on.

142
00:14:51,550 --> 00:14:52,950
Or you'll really be late.

143
00:14:55,840 --> 00:14:57,370
When did you add a seat to it?

144
00:14:58,350 --> 00:14:59,310
None of your business.

145
00:14:59,311 --> 00:15:00,770
I put it on when I wanted to.

146
00:15:01,840 --> 00:15:03,770
I don't really want to know anyway.

147
00:15:17,770 --> 00:15:19,030
Yun Li, you have a cold?

148
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:22,820
I'm fine.

149
00:15:22,821 --> 00:15:23,889
Drink some warm water, and I'll be fine.

150
00:15:23,890 --> 00:15:25,249
Then take care and get some good rest.

151
00:15:25,250 --> 00:15:26,250
Thank you, Qian.

152
00:15:52,930 --> 00:15:53,930
See you around.
Bye-bye.

153
00:15:58,100 --> 00:16:00,810
Take 2 pills at a time.

154
00:16:05,360 --> 00:16:06,690
The materials are ready

155
00:16:06,710 --> 00:16:08,200
for your review, sir.

156
00:16:21,790 --> 00:16:22,999
That place offers really delicious food.

157
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:23,820
I made a reservation

158
00:16:23,821 --> 00:16:25,869
right after you mentioned it last time.

159
00:16:25,870 --> 00:16:26,870
Okay, bye-bye.

160
00:16:27,200 --> 00:16:28,510
Yun Li, I'm off.

161
00:16:28,580 --> 00:16:29,960
-Bye-bye. -Bye-bye.

162
00:16:30,110 --> 00:16:31,160
I'm off. Bye-bye.

163
00:16:45,220 --> 00:16:47,169
You still haven't finished this yet?

164
00:16:47,170 --> 00:16:48,970
You're too inefficient, Yun Li.

165
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:51,270
I only have one page to go.

166
00:16:51,290 --> 00:16:52,409
You still need

167
00:16:52,410 --> 00:16:54,270
to improve your work efficiency.

168
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:56,549
You can't always do ineffective overtime.

169
00:16:56,550 --> 00:16:57,550
At this rate,

170
00:16:57,770 --> 00:16:59,369
how can I approve your overtime pay?

171
00:16:59,370 --> 00:17:00,370
I...
Mr. Qin,

172
00:17:00,460 --> 00:17:02,790
I don't think I asked for any overtime pay.

173
00:17:03,580 --> 00:17:04,580
I forgot that interns

174
00:17:05,380 --> 00:17:07,180
don't have overtime pay anyway.

175
00:17:08,569 --> 00:17:10,180
But I like your attitude.

176
00:17:10,460 --> 00:17:12,159
You're surely going to get

177
00:17:12,160 --> 00:17:13,348
the only regular position.

178
00:17:13,349 --> 00:17:14,349
Do your best.

179
00:17:34,980 --> 00:17:35,980
It's done.

180
00:17:44,180 --> 00:17:45,270
Well, Mr. Qin.

181
00:17:46,110 --> 00:17:47,750
I've wrapped it up.
I'm leaving them here.

182
00:17:47,980 --> 00:17:49,300
I'm getting off work now.
Hold on.

183
00:17:50,270 --> 00:17:51,509
This batch of purchase orders

184
00:17:51,510 --> 00:17:53,379
needs to be sorted out and
entered into the system again.

185
00:17:53,380 --> 00:17:54,840
Get it done for me tonight.

186
00:17:56,190 --> 00:17:58,400
Do they have to be submitted tonight?

187
00:17:58,460 --> 00:18:00,249
We're in urgent need of
them for tomorrow's meeting.

188
00:18:00,250 --> 00:18:01,910
I have no other choice either.

189
00:18:03,220 --> 00:18:04,220
How about this?

190
00:18:04,610 --> 00:18:05,610
I'll stay here with you.

191
00:18:05,611 --> 00:18:07,610
Give them to me whenever you finish.

192
00:18:10,460 --> 00:18:11,460
Get back to work.

193
00:18:46,380 --> 00:18:47,180
Never mind,

194
00:18:47,350 --> 00:18:49,950
at least he's willing
to work overtime with me.

195
00:19:40,770 --> 00:19:41,770
No way.

196
00:19:41,830 --> 00:19:43,430
I can't just put up with this.

197
00:19:56,380 --> 00:19:57,380
Is it fun?

198
00:20:00,090 --> 00:20:01,750
Aren't you going to continue?

199
00:20:02,180 --> 00:20:03,180
Fu,

200
00:20:03,240 --> 00:20:04,269
we're on the same team.

201
00:20:04,270 --> 00:20:05,270
Cut me some slack.

202
00:20:06,090 --> 00:20:07,820
Which group should I send it to?

203
00:20:12,270 --> 00:20:13,270
Mr. Qin,

204
00:20:14,630 --> 00:20:16,720
I need to talk to you.

205
00:20:19,740 --> 00:20:20,740
Go ahead.

206
00:20:21,380 --> 00:20:22,050
I think

207
00:20:22,051 --> 00:20:23,379
the work you assigned me today

208
00:20:23,380 --> 00:20:24,640
is very unreasonable.

209
00:20:24,790 --> 00:20:25,979
This work doesn't have

210
00:20:25,980 --> 00:20:27,400
to be completed today.

211
00:20:27,930 --> 00:20:29,569
You said you'd stay late with me,

212
00:20:29,570 --> 00:20:30,829
and I thought you needed

213
00:20:30,830 --> 00:20:31,570
the purchase materials urgently,

214
00:20:31,571 --> 00:20:33,199
but you turned out to be playing games.

215
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:34,289
In the end, I got it done

216
00:20:34,290 --> 00:20:35,330
all by myself.

217
00:20:36,940 --> 00:20:37,940
Yun Li!

218
00:20:38,440 --> 00:20:39,240
I was just trying

219
00:20:39,241 --> 00:20:40,939
to give you more opportunities!

220
00:20:40,940 --> 00:20:41,980
You've forced work onto me

221
00:20:42,480 --> 00:20:43,959
that I'm not responsible for.

222
00:20:43,960 --> 00:20:44,720
You young people

223
00:20:44,721 --> 00:20:46,659
shouldn't always make a
big deal out of everything.

224
00:20:46,660 --> 00:20:48,940
Everyone has been through this.

225
00:20:56,350 --> 00:20:57,350
Forget it.

226
00:20:57,380 --> 00:20:58,510
You can get off work.

227
00:20:58,610 --> 00:20:59,940
I'll do the rest myself.

228
00:21:03,400 --> 00:21:04,400
Take your things.

229
00:21:15,850 --> 00:21:16,850
Fu Shize.

230
00:21:17,880 --> 00:21:18,880
Thank you.

231
00:21:19,850 --> 00:21:20,850
Thank me for what?

232
00:21:21,490 --> 00:21:23,270
Thank you for helping me out.

233
00:21:24,320 --> 00:21:25,569
Thankfully, you were there with me.

234
00:21:25,570 --> 00:21:26,270
I just

235
00:21:26,271 --> 00:21:28,070
blurted it all out back there...

236
00:21:30,250 --> 00:21:31,719
If I have to say it again now,

237
00:21:31,720 --> 00:21:33,250
I'll definitely stutter.

238
00:21:37,140 --> 00:21:39,600
Weren't you off work already?

239
00:21:39,680 --> 00:21:41,810
What made you come back all of a sudden?

240
00:21:42,530 --> 00:21:43,420
Xia said it was so late,

241
00:21:43,421 --> 00:21:44,459
and you hadn't returned yet.

242
00:21:44,460 --> 00:21:45,520
She was so worried.

243
00:21:46,050 --> 00:21:47,480
I'll text Xia.

244
00:21:50,310 --> 00:21:52,180
M-My phone is dead.

245
00:21:52,350 --> 00:21:53,070
Can you help me

246
00:21:53,071 --> 00:21:54,510
tell Xia?

247
00:21:54,610 --> 00:21:55,610
Tell her what?

248
00:21:56,240 --> 00:21:58,370
Just tell her we are already together.

249
00:22:05,350 --> 00:22:07,350
I mean we have already...

250
00:22:08,420 --> 00:22:10,550
m-met up.

251
00:22:16,160 --> 00:22:17,399
Yun Li was working overtime in the office.

252
00:22:17,400 --> 00:22:18,070
She's fine.

253
00:22:18,250 --> 00:22:19,910
Let's go. I'll give you a ride.

254
00:22:26,700 --> 00:22:29,310
I want to go for a walk. May I?

255
00:22:31,090 --> 00:22:32,420
Are you feeling better?

256
00:22:33,350 --> 00:22:34,350
Much better.

257
00:22:34,830 --> 00:22:35,830
Mm.

258
00:22:44,270 --> 00:22:45,470
This looks so pretty.

259
00:23:01,920 --> 00:23:02,960
Hey, welcome!

260
00:23:02,990 --> 00:23:04,850
See if there's anything you like.

261
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:09,980
Hold on, hold on, miss.

262
00:23:13,510 --> 00:23:14,370
Check this out.

263
00:23:14,500 --> 00:23:15,659
Here are our little fairy sparklers,

264
00:23:15,660 --> 00:23:17,860
which suit fairies like you perfectly.

265
00:23:21,920 --> 00:23:22,920
No, thank you.

266
00:23:22,960 --> 00:23:23,960
We want a box.
Okay.

267
00:23:31,820 --> 00:23:32,820
Paid.
Okay, thank you.

268
00:23:38,440 --> 00:23:39,010
Hey there,

269
00:23:39,011 --> 00:23:40,269
see if there's anything you like.

270
00:23:40,270 --> 00:23:42,070
We offer all sorts of items here.

271
00:23:44,090 --> 00:23:46,479
During one Mid-Autumn
Festival when I was a kid,

272
00:23:46,480 --> 00:23:48,349
I spent all my savings

273
00:23:48,350 --> 00:23:49,379
buying plenty of fireworks

274
00:23:49,380 --> 00:23:50,840
to set off with my brother.

275
00:23:50,940 --> 00:23:51,750
But they ended up being

276
00:23:51,751 --> 00:23:53,739
confiscated by the city inspectors.

277
00:23:53,740 --> 00:23:56,400
It was indeed not very
safe to set off fireworks.

278
00:23:58,090 --> 00:23:59,630
Can we light them here?

279
00:24:01,010 --> 00:24:02,010
Mm.

280
00:24:08,010 --> 00:24:09,010
Come closer.

281
00:24:22,200 --> 00:24:23,330
I mean the sparkler.

282
00:24:43,330 --> 00:24:44,480
It's so beautiful.

283
00:25:18,790 --> 00:25:19,829
I could have drawn

284
00:25:19,830 --> 00:25:20,940
a great work.

285
00:25:21,220 --> 00:25:22,220
Try again.

286
00:25:25,900 --> 00:25:27,110
Have you tried it before?

287
00:25:28,610 --> 00:25:29,610
Mm,

288
00:25:29,750 --> 00:25:31,430
with my childhood friend when I was a kid.

289
00:25:32,880 --> 00:25:33,880
Mr. Xu?

290
00:25:37,240 --> 00:25:39,440
My only childhood friend is my brother.

291
00:25:45,680 --> 00:25:46,680
You get one, too.

292
00:25:47,330 --> 00:25:48,790
Have fun together with me.

293
00:25:59,850 --> 00:26:00,920
You draw one, too!

294
00:26:01,960 --> 00:26:02,640
Draw what?

295
00:26:02,960 --> 00:26:04,480
Draw whatever you want.

296
00:26:28,420 --> 00:26:29,900
May I borrow your phone?

297
00:26:52,220 --> 00:26:53,790
Remember to send me the photos.

298
00:26:54,180 --> 00:26:55,180
Mm.

299
00:27:00,070 --> 00:27:01,010
Today is the happiest day

300
00:27:01,011 --> 00:27:02,240
I've had this year.

301
00:27:04,550 --> 00:27:05,880
The year isn't over yet.

302
00:27:07,110 --> 00:27:08,110
Then tell me.

303
00:27:08,540 --> 00:27:09,150
Do you remember

304
00:27:09,151 --> 00:27:11,010
what you did on this day last year?

305
00:27:14,500 --> 00:27:15,500
Me neither.

306
00:27:15,960 --> 00:27:16,350
But

307
00:27:16,351 --> 00:27:17,919
next year, I'll definitely remember

308
00:27:17,920 --> 00:27:20,050
what I did today.

309
00:28:00,720 --> 00:28:02,269
Thank you for seeing me home.

310
00:28:02,270 --> 00:28:03,270
Mm.

311
00:28:04,380 --> 00:28:05,910
Remember to take your meds.

312
00:28:06,350 --> 00:28:07,700
Mm, okay.

313
00:28:14,900 --> 00:28:15,900
Go back inside.

314
00:28:16,700 --> 00:28:17,700
Mm.

315
00:28:21,810 --> 00:28:22,810
By the way...

316
00:28:23,530 --> 00:28:25,790
There's one more thing I want to tell you.

317
00:28:30,180 --> 00:28:31,180
Go ahead.

318
00:28:39,960 --> 00:28:42,720
Is it something important?

319
00:28:44,050 --> 00:28:45,250
It's very important.

320
00:28:52,440 --> 00:28:53,440
Actually...

321
00:28:56,200 --> 00:28:58,090
A-Actually, I...

322
00:29:03,770 --> 00:29:05,030
I am the same age as you.

323
00:29:12,880 --> 00:29:14,269
I-If you don't believe me,

324
00:29:14,270 --> 00:29:15,850
I can show you my ID card.

325
00:29:17,250 --> 00:29:18,250
I believe you.

326
00:29:25,430 --> 00:29:26,960
What month were you born in?

327
00:29:27,660 --> 00:29:28,660
February.

328
00:29:30,480 --> 00:29:32,480
I'm only one month younger than you.

329
00:29:32,940 --> 00:29:33,880
So you don't have

330
00:29:33,881 --> 00:29:36,140
to treat me as a junior
and take care of me.

331
00:29:38,070 --> 00:29:39,800
Then what should I treat you as?

332
00:29:41,180 --> 00:29:42,980
A... friend?

333
00:29:56,280 --> 00:29:57,340
You freaked me out.

334
00:29:57,960 --> 00:29:59,960
Tangy, what are you doing here?

335
00:30:00,270 --> 00:30:01,610
Lili, you're back.

336
00:30:02,610 --> 00:30:04,740
Have you gotten better from your cold?

337
00:30:06,350 --> 00:30:08,026
Thanks to your medicine,
I'm much better now.

338
00:30:08,050 --> 00:30:09,050
What medicine?

339
00:30:09,460 --> 00:30:10,380
Cold medicine, of course!

340
00:30:10,381 --> 00:30:11,910
The one you left on my table.

341
00:30:11,960 --> 00:30:13,110
I didn't do it.

342
00:30:13,250 --> 00:30:14,250
You didn't?

343
00:30:16,210 --> 00:30:17,210
Was it Fu Shize?

344
00:30:17,750 --> 00:30:19,280
Remember to take your meds.

345
00:30:25,460 --> 00:30:26,110
Did anything

346
00:30:26,111 --> 00:30:27,460
happen between you two?

347
00:30:27,510 --> 00:30:28,510
Come on, spill it.

348
00:30:29,420 --> 00:30:30,420
Well...

349
00:30:32,660 --> 00:30:33,570
Today, Mr. Qin

350
00:30:33,590 --> 00:30:35,749
made me work overtime deliberately, right?

351
00:30:35,750 --> 00:30:37,550
And then Fu Shize stood up for me.

352
00:30:37,610 --> 00:30:39,679
He also went for a walk with me,

353
00:30:39,680 --> 00:30:40,979
lit sparklers,

354
00:30:40,980 --> 00:30:42,569
and sent me back.

355
00:30:42,570 --> 00:30:43,660
Not bad!

356
00:30:43,960 --> 00:30:45,220
What a rich itinerary!

357
00:30:48,660 --> 00:30:50,009
So you came back so late

358
00:30:50,010 --> 00:30:51,459
because you went on a date?

359
00:30:51,460 --> 00:30:53,069
N-No, it doesn't count as a date.

360
00:30:53,070 --> 00:30:54,070
Um...

361
00:30:54,550 --> 00:30:56,049
A guy and a girl were alone together

362
00:30:56,050 --> 00:30:56,980
this late at night,

363
00:30:56,981 --> 00:30:58,049
lighting sparklers?

364
00:30:58,050 --> 00:30:59,780
What else could it be but a date?

365
00:31:00,250 --> 00:31:01,250
Tell me.

366
00:31:01,510 --> 00:31:02,840
How far have things gone

367
00:31:02,880 --> 00:31:04,610
between you two now?

368
00:31:05,160 --> 00:31:06,480
We've made it clear.

369
00:31:06,960 --> 00:31:07,680
We are now

370
00:31:07,681 --> 00:31:09,270
officially friends!

371
00:31:10,720 --> 00:31:11,750
Just friends?

372
00:31:13,320 --> 00:31:15,300
I've already made great strides.

373
00:31:15,320 --> 00:31:17,520
At least he no longer sees me as a junior.

374
00:31:17,590 --> 00:31:18,400
I'm already happy

375
00:31:18,401 --> 00:31:20,350
being friends with him.

376
00:31:20,510 --> 00:31:22,550
You're happy with so little!

377
00:31:23,500 --> 00:31:26,200
There's a whole galaxy

378
00:31:26,310 --> 00:31:28,640
between "just friend" and "girlfriend."

379
00:31:31,010 --> 00:31:33,260
I've already done a 100-meter sprint.

380
00:31:33,290 --> 00:31:35,399
I should at least be
allowed to catch my breath.

381
00:31:35,400 --> 00:31:36,400
No way.

382
00:31:36,920 --> 00:31:38,289
You're at the starting line now,

383
00:31:38,290 --> 00:31:39,719
still so far from the finish line.

384
00:31:39,720 --> 00:31:41,720
You must sprint with all your might.

385
00:31:41,810 --> 00:31:44,719
Love is about timing. You have to
act when there are good feelings,

386
00:31:44,720 --> 00:31:46,900
turning a friend

387
00:31:47,090 --> 00:31:49,150
into a boyfriend as soon as possible.

388
00:31:50,750 --> 00:31:52,460
Should I court him then?

389
00:31:52,500 --> 00:31:53,500
Yes, of course.

390
00:31:53,590 --> 00:31:54,720
You must pursue him.

391
00:31:55,180 --> 00:31:57,440
You're pursuing this moon in your heart.

392
00:31:58,330 --> 00:32:00,399
How high do you think my chances

393
00:32:00,400 --> 00:32:01,900
of success are?

394
00:32:02,090 --> 00:32:03,700
Probably about...

395
00:32:05,270 --> 00:32:06,440
0.1%.

396
00:32:06,770 --> 00:32:07,770
This low?

397
00:32:09,500 --> 00:32:10,200
Forget it.

398
00:32:10,201 --> 00:32:11,589
I'm not going to embarrass myself.

399
00:32:11,590 --> 00:32:13,529
I'm happy just being friends with him.

400
00:32:13,530 --> 00:32:15,060
Let's just leave it at that.

401
00:32:15,680 --> 00:32:16,620
No!

402
00:32:16,700 --> 00:32:18,560
How will you know if you don't try?

403
00:32:18,820 --> 00:32:19,620
By the way,

404
00:32:19,700 --> 00:32:20,680
didn't he say last time

405
00:32:20,681 --> 00:32:22,739
that the crepe rolls
you made were really good?

406
00:32:22,740 --> 00:32:24,239
How about you make some more for him?

407
00:32:24,240 --> 00:32:25,070
I asked him about it,

408
00:32:25,071 --> 00:32:26,140
and he said no.

409
00:32:26,290 --> 00:32:27,950
He said no, so you just give up?

410
00:32:28,030 --> 00:32:29,479
If you just make them

411
00:32:29,480 --> 00:32:30,789
and put them in front of him,

412
00:32:30,790 --> 00:32:31,920
could he refuse you?

413
00:32:33,200 --> 00:32:33,980
You're so right.

414
00:32:33,981 --> 00:32:35,289
I'll make crepe rolls tomorrow

415
00:32:35,290 --> 00:32:36,490
and bring them to him.

416
00:32:36,900 --> 00:32:37,900
That's right.

417
00:32:37,980 --> 00:32:39,569
The way to a man's heart

418
00:32:39,570 --> 00:32:41,180
is through his stomach.

419
00:32:45,960 --> 00:32:47,200
Enough about me.

420
00:32:47,270 --> 00:32:48,270
What about you?

421
00:32:48,530 --> 00:32:49,939
You give me advice every day,

422
00:32:49,940 --> 00:32:51,400
but are you dating anyone?

423
00:32:51,980 --> 00:32:53,639
You're not getting any younger.

424
00:32:53,640 --> 00:32:55,500
It's time for you to date someone.

425
00:32:56,460 --> 00:32:58,920
What do you mean I'm
not getting any younger?

426
00:32:59,770 --> 00:33:01,180
I'm in my prime!

427
00:33:01,400 --> 00:33:03,199
I'm just waiting to meet the right person

428
00:33:03,200 --> 00:33:04,330
at the right time.

429
00:33:04,590 --> 00:33:06,589
I'd rather date no one than
settle for less, you know?

430
00:33:06,590 --> 00:33:08,199
You'd rather date no
one than settle for less.

431
00:33:08,200 --> 00:33:09,440
Let's drop it.
I'm heading home.

432
00:33:11,440 --> 00:33:12,440
Rest early, huh?

433
00:33:41,240 --> 00:33:42,240
Photo received.

434
00:33:51,610 --> 00:33:53,240
I had a great time today.

435
00:33:53,740 --> 00:33:55,200
Get some good rest.

436
00:33:55,460 --> 00:33:56,460
Good night.

437
00:35:04,820 --> 00:35:07,280
Don't have iced coffee only in the morning.

438
00:35:07,380 --> 00:35:09,640
Eat some breakfast to fill your stomach.

439
00:35:30,010 --> 00:35:31,379
Hello, anyone from Engineering?

440
00:35:31,380 --> 00:35:32,819
The expression tester is malfunctioning.

441
00:35:32,820 --> 00:35:33,959
Could someone from Engineering

442
00:35:33,960 --> 00:35:35,290
come over and repair it?

443
00:35:38,820 --> 00:35:39,550
Engineer Fu,

444
00:35:39,551 --> 00:35:41,550
the machine's screen is glitching.

445
00:35:41,590 --> 00:35:42,590
Let me check.

446
00:35:55,270 --> 00:35:56,270
You know what?

447
00:35:56,300 --> 00:35:57,419
You made the right choice

448
00:35:57,420 --> 00:35:58,820
joining our skateboard club.
Really?

449
00:35:59,090 --> 00:36:00,939
I've been skateboarding for 7 years.

450
00:36:00,940 --> 00:36:02,049
I'm really good at it.

451
00:36:02,050 --> 00:36:02,570
No way,

452
00:36:02,780 --> 00:36:03,859
I must figure out a way

453
00:36:03,860 --> 00:36:05,299
and not let someone else get to him first.

454
00:36:05,300 --> 00:36:06,300
Feel free to ask me anytime

455
00:36:06,301 --> 00:36:07,649
if you have any questions.

456
00:36:07,650 --> 00:36:08,650
Great.
Thank you, senior.

457
00:36:09,010 --> 00:36:10,210
That's so nice of you.

458
00:36:12,690 --> 00:36:14,089
His level is just average.

459
00:36:14,090 --> 00:36:15,890
Anyone who can skate can do that.

460
00:36:16,400 --> 00:36:17,529
I am indeed average.

461
00:36:17,530 --> 00:36:19,026
But as long as you
come to our skateboard club more often

462
00:36:19,050 --> 00:36:19,570
and practice more,

463
00:36:19,571 --> 00:36:20,939
you will become extraordinary.

464
00:36:20,940 --> 00:36:21,690
Cut the crap.

465
00:36:21,691 --> 00:36:22,890
Are we leaving or not?

466
00:36:22,900 --> 00:36:24,626
I got my skateboard.
So don't worry about me.

467
00:36:24,650 --> 00:36:26,436
Remember to come to our club
for more practice.

468
00:36:26,460 --> 00:36:27,526
Okay.
- Thank you, senior. -Thank you.

469
00:36:27,550 --> 00:36:28,750
-Bye-bye. -Bye-bye.

470
00:36:31,690 --> 00:36:32,500
Finally, people won't

471
00:36:32,501 --> 00:36:34,230
judge me or laugh at me anymore.

472
00:36:45,670 --> 00:36:47,150
Why didn't he eat any?

473
00:36:48,920 --> 00:36:50,450
Someone from Engineering,

474
00:36:51,110 --> 00:36:53,040
bring the engineering board over.

475
00:37:01,720 --> 00:37:02,830
Hello, Fu Shize.

476
00:37:03,710 --> 00:37:04,780
I'm Yun Li.

477
00:37:04,810 --> 00:37:06,429
I'm at your engineering department.

478
00:37:06,430 --> 00:37:07,830
There's no one else here.

479
00:37:07,980 --> 00:37:09,336
What item do you need?
Where is it?

480
00:37:09,360 --> 00:37:10,490
I'll bring it to you.

481
00:37:27,690 --> 00:37:28,690
Fu Shize.

482
00:37:32,470 --> 00:37:33,670
Is this what you need?

483
00:37:34,730 --> 00:37:35,730
Mm.

484
00:37:41,210 --> 00:37:43,050
Why didn't you eat breakfast?

485
00:37:43,860 --> 00:37:45,590
It's not good for your stomach.

486
00:37:46,420 --> 00:37:48,020
I haven't had time to eat yet.

487
00:37:54,820 --> 00:37:55,820
Thank you.

488
00:37:59,010 --> 00:38:00,759
You left that cold medicine on my table

489
00:38:00,760 --> 00:38:01,960
yesterday, right?

490
00:38:03,130 --> 00:38:04,130
Mm.

491
00:38:07,510 --> 00:38:08,510
Thank you.

492
00:38:18,130 --> 00:38:20,260
What is this? I haven't seen it before.

493
00:38:20,460 --> 00:38:22,590
Welcome to try the expression tester.

494
00:38:22,880 --> 00:38:24,810
Please scan the code on the screen.

495
00:38:28,000 --> 00:38:29,629
I can rate your mood today

496
00:38:29,630 --> 00:38:30,959
based on

497
00:38:30,960 --> 00:38:32,020
your expressions.

498
00:38:33,630 --> 00:38:36,370
Please follow the prompt
and make an expression.

499
00:38:36,690 --> 00:38:38,190
Elated.

500
00:38:42,570 --> 00:38:44,340
You scored a total of 20 points.

501
00:38:44,550 --> 00:38:45,590
You failed.

502
00:38:46,570 --> 00:38:48,770
It seems that you are in a bad mood today.

503
00:38:48,860 --> 00:38:50,420
Please try again.

504
00:38:57,500 --> 00:38:58,609
Your smile beats

505
00:38:58,610 --> 00:39:00,070
99% of all smiles.

506
00:39:06,510 --> 00:39:08,710
This machine hasn't been repaired yet.

507
00:39:09,400 --> 00:39:11,060
I think it's a bit inaccurate.

508
00:39:13,630 --> 00:39:14,630
Inaccurate?

509
00:39:15,070 --> 00:39:16,070
Mm.

510
00:39:22,840 --> 00:39:25,630
Prompt, overjoyed.

511
00:39:27,610 --> 00:39:29,650
You scored a total of 10 points.

512
00:39:29,940 --> 00:39:31,840
You beat 5% of people.

513
00:39:32,670 --> 00:39:33,500
Cutie,

514
00:39:33,610 --> 00:39:35,419
you look a bit expressionless today.

515
00:39:35,420 --> 00:39:37,420
Remember to keep smiling.

516
00:39:40,500 --> 00:39:42,530
You scored a total of 10 points.

517
00:39:42,820 --> 00:39:44,710
You beat 5% of people.

518
00:39:45,150 --> 00:39:45,980
Cutie,

519
00:39:46,150 --> 00:39:47,759
you look a bit expressionless today.

520
00:39:47,760 --> 00:39:49,860
Remember to keep smiling.

521
00:39:53,360 --> 00:39:54,360
It's inaccurate.

522
00:39:54,610 --> 00:39:56,480
Yes, it is inaccurate.

523
00:39:56,510 --> 00:39:58,970
We need to get the
manufacturer to repair it.

524
00:40:07,230 --> 00:40:09,670
Overjoyed, 100 points!

525
00:40:10,120 --> 00:40:11,120
Cutie,

526
00:40:11,150 --> 00:40:12,399
are you the happiest person

527
00:40:12,400 --> 00:40:13,590
in the world?

528
00:40:16,340 --> 00:40:19,230
Actually, 5% is pretty good.

529
00:40:19,340 --> 00:40:20,740
Think about it. Even 5%
of the total

530
00:40:21,110 --> 00:40:22,730
is still a very large number.

531
00:40:24,840 --> 00:40:26,300
You're quite optimistic.

532
00:40:27,110 --> 00:40:27,920
Life is

533
00:40:27,921 --> 00:40:29,520
all about being optimistic.

534
00:40:30,170 --> 00:40:31,430
You should smile more.

535
00:40:32,510 --> 00:40:33,820
You look good when you smile.

